# evidence
ev("Jaryd (3) went missing Oct 2, 1999 hiking the Big South Trail in Roosevelt National Forest with his 6-year-old sister and 11 Christian Singles Network members; his father was not on the hike; the group had said it would only go to the fish hatchery.",
   ["P001","P002","P003","O003","E001","E002","L001","L010","L012",r_disv,r_disloc,r_lsw,r_hike1,r_hike2,r_hike3,r_hikeloc,r_hatch,r_sib,r_child,r_mem],"COL19")
ev("Poudre River Resort was owned by Allyn and his twin brother Arlyn; Allyn was divorced from the children's mother; trail 15 miles west of resort, 60 miles west of Fort Collins, trail 11 miles, 8,440 ft, Comanche Peak Wilderness.",
   ["P004","L003",r_own1,r_own2,r_twin,"L009",r_trail1],"COL19")
ev("SAR timeline: 10 a.m. group leaves resort; 11:30 two fishermen talk to Jaryd near Camp 2 and see group 50-80 ft away (last known to see him); ~12:15 group realizes he is missing and searches ~1 hr; ~4 p.m. Allyn calls 911, resort manager already had; 4:26 page to Bill Nelson; 5:07 page to SAR manager George Janson.",
   ["E003","E005","E006","P016","P017","L004","P009","P014","P030",r_fish1,r_fish2,r_fishE,r_fishE2,r_lastloc,r_e5,r_rep,r_rep2,r_dep,r_jansonO,"D001",r_sar,r_sar2],"COL19")
ev("Some hikers reported hearing a scream; Josallyn told her father it sounded like a playful scream.",["E004",r_scream,r_scream2],"COL19")
ev("Bill Nelson (later undersheriff) was in charge of the search; Justin Smith was a sergeant and the search PIO, now sheriff.",["P009","P010",r_nelson,r_smith,r_nelsonO,r_smithO],"COL19")
ev("Oct 3, 1999: Air Force Huey UH-1N from F.E. Warren AFB refueled at Fort Collins-Loveland airport, then crashed ~3:30 p.m. during low hovering search on upper Big South Trail with 4 Air Force members and SAR member Mark Sheets; all survived, two with significant injuries; Sheets spent 3 days at Poudre Valley Hospital.",
   ["V001","O008","E008","L007","L014","P013","L020",r_heli,r_helio,r_sheets,r_crashloc,r_refuel,r_hosp,r_srch4],"COL19")
ev("Oct 4, 1999: a Lama helicopter from GeoSeis Helicopters encountered swirling winds and returned to Fort Collins. Oct 5-7: 200+ trained searchers, a dozen dog teams, trackers, a dive team and a plane searched. Oct 8, 7 p.m.: search suspended.",
   ["V002","O010","E027","V003","E007","E010",r_lama,r_lamao,r_plane,r_srch2,r_river,r_susp2,"L008"],"COL19")
ev("June 4, 2003: Gary Watts and Rob Osborne found a white Tarzan tennis shoe, the other shoe, a brown fleece jacket and blue sweatpants turned inside out on a talus slope ~500 vertical feet (1,050 lateral feet) above the trail near Camp 2; jacket had apparent puncture marks; shoes little weathering.",
   ["P007","P008","E014","L005","X001","X002","X003",r_find1,r_find2,r_findloc,r_x1,r_x2,r_x3],"COL19")
ev("June 5, 2003: the hikers took photos and items to LCSO; photos emailed to Allyn, who confirmed the clothing and shoes were Jaryd's.",["E015","E028",r_turn,r_turn2,r_id,r_x1o,r_x2o,r_x3o],"COL19")
ev("June 14, 2003: LCSO, Larimer County SAR, Division of Wildlife and NecroSearch (later joined by Allyn and the local Child Protection Network) found a skull fragment in a crevice and a tooth on a log, ~180 ft north and ~20 ft higher than the clothing site, at ~9,120 ft.",
   ["E017","O005","O011","L006","X004","X005",r_rec1,r_rec2,r_rec3,r_rec4,r_rec5,r_recloc,r_x4,r_x5,r_trail8],"COL19")
ev("SAR member Don Davis recalled the skull being spotted under a shrub; initial DNA tests showed 86% likelihood; a decade later new DNA technology proved 100%.",["P015","E018",r_rec6,r_davisO,r_x4id],"COL19")
ev("CBI tests of the clothing (blood, hair) revealed little; death certificate lists manner 'undetermined, probable mountain lion attack'.",["O006","D003","X006",r_hair2,r_dc2,r_cbiinv,"D009",r_dna1,r_dna4],"COL19")
ev("Investigators questioned Allyn, group members, fishermen and the children's mother; Smith and Nelson said abduction was improbable; both believe a mountain lion killed Jaryd quickly.",["O001","O002",r_resp,r_srch1,r_srchloc],"COL19")
